1279:| `worktree_isolation_requires_local_board` | The resolved board is remote. Every managed-workspace surface refuses before any side effect. |
1280:| `worktree_not_a_git_repository` | The control root is not inside a Git working tree, so a repository-mutating producer has nothing to isolate in. |
1281:| `worktree_protected_authority_unavailable` | The unique authorized repository binding or its fresh remote HEAD/exact-ref fetch cannot be read. Restore remote access; local or cached authority is never substituted. |
1282:| `worktree_protected_authority_indeterminate` | Repository binding or fresh remote evidence is ambiguous, malformed, incomplete, unreadable after fetch, or disagrees by OID. Repair the evidence; no candidate is authorized. |
1283:| `worktree_configured_trunk_not_protected_default` | The optional configured branch/tracking pair differs from the independently resolved protected branch/remote pair. Align or remove the pin; configuration cannot select authority. |
1284:| `worktree_trunk_ambiguous` | Compatibility-only `ResolveTrunk` advisory discovery found no unique candidate (or a no-remote checkout had detached `HEAD`); it is not a protected-authority provisioning outcome. |
1285:| `worktree_integration_base_missing` | Compatibility-only `ResolveTrunk` could positively establish that its named local base ref is missing; authority-sensitive callers do not use this as a fallback. |
1286:| `worktree_trunk_authority_unresolved` | Compatibility-only `ResolveTrunk` could not establish tracking/cache authority; unknown is never treated as absent. |
1287:| `worktree_trunk_authority_refresh_failed` | Compatibility-only `ResolveTrunk` could not refresh or resolve its configured upstream. |
1288:| `worktree_trunk_local_ahead_of_authority` | Compatibility-only `ResolveTrunk` found unpublished local commits. Fresh protected-authority provisioning does not read or reject the local branch for this relation. |
1289:| `worktree_trunk_diverged_from_authority` | Compatibility-only `ResolveTrunk` found local/upstream divergence. Fresh protected-authority provisioning seeds from the fetched OID without rewriting the local checkout. |
1290:| `worktree_branch_collision` | `task-board/story/<STORY-ID>` exists but is not a workspace task-board owns. |
1291:| `worktree_path_collision` | The managed path is occupied by something task-board did not create. |
1292:| `worktree_ownership_mismatch` | A workspace record names a different repository, Story, branch, path, or client. |
1293:| `worktree_lease_unavailable` | Another run holds the Story lease and is live or unclassifiable. Ordinarily a scheduling condition; on `abort` and `repair` it is a refusal to race a writer. |
1294:| `worktree_git_command_failed` | A Git read this decision depends on failed, so the state is unknown rather than absent. Repair refuses; cleanup stays blocked. |
1295:| `worktree_path_unreadable` | The managed path could not be read (permissions, I/O, an unmounted volume), so its presence is unknown rather than absent. Carries the errno. Nothing is created, cleared, or removed on it. |
1296:| `worktree_ref_unreadable` | A Git ref lookup failed, so the ref's existence is unknown rather than missing — an unreadable loose ref or `packed-refs`, an unreadable base commit, an ancestry probe that exited fatal, or a Git too old for `show-ref --exists`. Carries Git's own diagnostic. Provisioning, `repair`, `cleanup`, and `abort --discard` all refuse on it; nothing is branched, added, removed, or attested. |
1297:| `worktree_missing` / `worktree_stale` | The worktree or branch is gone, or the branch no longer contains the recorded checkpoint. |
1298:| `worktree_cleanup_blocked` | A cleanup precondition is unmet; the workspace is retained. Includes a Story lease that could not be read: unknown blocks, because "I could not tell whether anyone is writing here" only supports assuming someone is. |
1299:| `worktree_abort_requires_confirmation` | `--discard` without `--confirm`. |
